y{node.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color}];}catch(e){}}if('children' in node)node.children.forEach(c=>tint(c,color));}\n```\n\nStockRow:\n```js\nasync function buildStockRow(){\n  const row=figma.createComponent();row.name='Stock Row';row.resize(327,64);row.fills=[];\n  const box=figma.createFrame();box.name='LogoBox';box.resize(40,40);box.x=0;box.y=12;box.cornerRadius=12;box.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:C.sf}];row.appendChild(box);\n  const lg=await I('3:116',box,10,8,20,24);lg.name='Logo';\n  await T(row,'NFLX',15,'S',C.ink,52,12).then(t=>t.name='Ticker');\n  await T(row,'Netflix, Inc',12,'R',C.sub,52,32).then(t=>t.name='Company');\n  const sp=V(row,'M0 12 L8 8 L16 11 L24 5 L32 9 L40 2',C.grn,168,26,1.5);sp.name='Spark';\n  const pr=await T(row,'$88.91',15,'S',C.ink,327-90,12,{w:90,align:'RIGHT'});pr.name='Price';\n  const ch=await T(row,'+1.29%',12,'S',C.grn,327-90,32,{w:90,align:'RIGHT'});ch.name='Change';\n  return row;\n}\n```\nWait: text name assignment — set t.name after creation. T returns node; name property settable.\n\nSpark: overwrite vectorPaths on instance children? Instance children are read-only except certain props? You CANNOT modify vectorPaths of nodes inside instances. But you CAN change fills/strokes. So per-instance spark variation: change stroke color only; shape stays same. Acceptable — but loss rows should trend down. Alternative: include two spark vectors in component: \"SparkUp\" and \"SparkDown\"; per instance set one invisible. \n\nWishRow: same minus price: LogoBox, Ticker, Company, Spark, Change (right, 14 S).\n\nChange text for wishlist rows: just \"−0.05%\" etc.\n\nIndexCard:\n```js\nconst card=figma.createComponent();card.name='Index Card';card.resize(160,88);card.cornerRadius=16;card.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:C.sf}];\nT(card,'S&P 500',16,'B',C.ink,14,12) name 'Name'\nT(card,'S&P · Standard & Poor’s',11,'R',C.sub,14,34) name 'Sub'\nchip: rounded rect green bg + text +49.50% at (14,54): R(card,14,54,72,22,C.grnBg,11); T(...,'+49.50%',12,'S'