e line). Highlight point \"Sep 27 · $88.04\": dot on line + tooltip label above.\n- Range selector: 1D 1W 1M 1Y 5Y ALL — pills; 1M active (brand bg white text).\n- View tabs: Summary / Details — Details active (underline or pill).\n- Financials: \"Financials\" header; tabs Revenue/Earnings/Performance (Revenue active); bar chart years 2018–2021: 4 bars with labels.\n- Bottom: Buy stocks button (primary instance, label \"Buy stocks\") — place above home indicator, maybe fixed: just place at y=812-34-52-12=714. Content above must fit: header 44+44=88; identity ~50 (y=96..146); price y=150..215; chart y=220..400 (180); ranges y=412..448; view tabs y=456..492; financials y=500..700 (header 24, tabs 32, bars 120). Tight but ok: financials bars y=580..690, button 714. Let me set chart 160 tall. I'll compute in code carefully.\n\nActually space is very tight. Option: put Buy button overlapping bottom with white bg bar. Fine.\n\n10_Confirm_Order:\n- Header: back + \"Confirm Order\".\n- Stock card: logo, NFLX, Netflix, Inc, $88.91 right.\n- Order summary card: rows: Funding source — Stockup; Approx share price — $88.91; Approx shares — 3; Fee — $2.10; divider; Total — $268.83 (bold).\n- \"Payment method\" label; two Payment Row instances: Debit Card (icon 3:146 default) with desc; Apple Pay: swap icon to 3:140, title \"Apple Pay\", desc \"Connect your Apple Pay account\". Neither chosen (default radio).\n- Confirm order button at bottom.\n\n11_Profile:\n- Header \"Profile\".\n- Avatar_Neutral 72×72, name \"Agatha Bella\", email.\n- Invite card: brand bg rounded, \"Invite friends\" bold white + \"Invite your friends and get $15\" white80 + maybe gift emoji? no emoji. Add \"$15\" badge.\n- Entries: Profile Row instances: Account, Security, Billing / Payments, Language (value \"English\"), Settings, FAQ.\n- Tab bar current Profile.\n\nPrototype links (batch 7):\n- 01_Splash → after delay 800ms → 02_Onboarding.\n- 02: Sign up button → 03_Empty; Skip → 03_Empty.\n- 03_Filled Continue → 04.\n- 04: back → 03_Filled; Send code → 05.\n- 05: back → 04; Verify account → 06.\n- 06: button → 07.\n- 07: portfolio value area → 08; NFLX stock row → 09; tabs Home→07,Portfolio→08,Trade→10,Market→none(entry only, no link? brief: tabs → 07/08/10/11 on 07; Market entry only so no link),Profile→11.\n- 08: back → 07; NFLX row → 09; tabs similarly.\n- 09: back → 07; Buy stocks → 10.\n- 10: back → 09; Confirm order → 07.\n- 11: tabs.\n\nTrigger nodes: for buttons inside instances, reactions go on the instance node. For tab bar tabs: reactions on the tab frames inside instance? Can't add reactions to nested children of instance? Reactions on instance children are allowed as overrides? Actually prototype interactions on nested nodes of instances can't be edited... You CAN add interactions to elements inside instances? In Figma, interactions on nested layers of instances are not allowed. Hmm — actually you can add prototype interactions to layers inside an instance? I believe no; only the instance itself and non-instance nodes. Let me instead: add invisible hot-spot rectangles on top of tab bar in each screen with reactions. That's simplest and robust: transparent rects (opacity 0? must have fill with opacity 0 to receive taps... In Figma, a rectangle with fills=[] won't trigger; use fill white 0.001 opacity? Use fills solid white with opacity 0 — prototype hit area still works if opacity 0? Yes, 0-opacity filled shapes still receive taps in prototypes.)\n\nSimilarly for stock rows: hotspot over NFLX row; portfolio value area hotspot.\n\nOK. Also remember each screen: status bar at top + home indicator at bottom.\n\nLet me now write batch 2 code. I need to re-declare helpers each call. To save tokens I'll keep helper code compact.\n\nPositions for frames:\nconst P={s1:[0,0],s2:[420,0],s3e:[840,0],s3f:[1260,0],s4:[1680,0],s5:[2100,0],s6:[0,880],s7:[420,880],s8:[840,880],s9:[1260,880],s10:[1680,880],s11:[2100,880]}.\n\nEach screen frame: 375×812, white fill, name e